  "raw_control_policy": "Before grading, independently verify both raw control checkpoints and train/valid prediction files against their source receipts and hashes, including existing output destinations. The supplied hashes bind known historical artifacts; if a file is missing or current hash differs, pause this comparison and recover/inspect the artifact rather than regenerating the raw recipe under this plan.",
  "profile_acceptance": "For each profile require PROFILE_UPDATE_EVIDENCE: attempts > 0; attempts = completed + AMP skips; loss_checks = attempts; loss finite; gradients finite by GradScaler found-inf flags after unscale; valid_for_throughput true. Capture full/reserved VRAM, cgroup/RSS/OOM events, phase timings, source/data identity. B8 first per seed; do B16 only after B8 receipts pass and cloud/device headroom review. B16 profiles remain conditional on the explicit 20% headroom gate in profile_gate; B8 success never auto-admits B16.",
  "allocation_gate": "The prepared sequence is seed3 then independent review/grade of its paired raw control, then seed4 only under fresh root admission and remaining authorized spend. Do not schedule both wide fits concurrently. The full two-seed design is preferred for seed variability but root may defer seed4 on opportunity cost without rejecting the mechanism.",
  "downstream_evidence": "Report per-seed full-vs-raw global_wp_clip2_v1 on the same exposed fold0, fit/throughput/resource deltas, residual correlation and any frozen teacher/student or blend contribution with ancestry. A weaker standalone member may still be conditionally useful; establish contribution with a fixed student/control recipe and identical evaluation unit before promotion.",
